University Budget Tracking System

A menu-driven Python project that manages university department budgets and financial transactions.


Features


Add departments and allocate budgets.

Record credit and debit transactions.

Update and delete transactions (CRUD).

Calculate department-wise credits, expenses, available funds and budget utilisation.

Save data in budget_data.json so it remains available after restarting.

Export transactions to transactions_export.csv for Excel / Power BI.


Requirements


Python 3.9 or newer

No external packages required.


Run

python budget_tracking_system.py

Example workflow


Add department: D01, Computer Science, 100000

Add a debit transaction: T01, D01, 15000, debit, Lab equipment

View financial overview.

Export the transactions to CSV.


How the calculation works

Available funds = Allocated budget + Total credits - Total debits


Budget utilised (%) = Total debits / Allocated budget * 100


In this sample application, a credit means additional funds received and a debit means spending. The project is an educational prototype, not an accounting or financial-control system.
